<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Suedzucker unit buys U.K. co.</title>
<headline>Belgian Suedzucker unit buys U.K. co.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian sugar company Raffinerie Tirlemontoise, a unit of Germany's Suedzucker group, said on Friday it had acquired British food company W.T. Mather Ltd.</p>
<p>W.T. Mather specialises in the supply of mincemeat and other preserves to the baking industry, Tirlemontoise said. Mather has annual sales of around nine million pounds sterling, it added.</p>
<p>Acquisition terms were not given.</p>
